# 103-demo-sections.lua

Builds each scene of the phase 1 demo on real home folders and returns a
record of what is on disk.  Prints nothing (`104-demo-view.lua` draws).
Loaded with `require("103-demo-sections")`.

## The context every scene takes

`ctx` is a table:

| field | type | meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `scratch` | string | folder the scene's homes are made under (cleared per scene) |
| `m` | table | the loaded modules: `rooms` (002), `tree` (021), `forest_text` (024), `recipients` (041), `people` (061), `log` (081) |
| `probes` | table | `102-demo-probes` |
| `baseline` | list of `{ key = string, value = string }` | every config key set in each new home before anything else |
| `variants_by_key` | table string → list of string | the variants a scene runs for its key; a key missing here is an error |
| `options`, `gather` | record, module | only the `tally` scene uses these |

## Outward functions (each takes `ctx`, gives a record)

| function | record fields |
|---|---|
| `flat(ctx)` | `home_dir`, `seconds_to_make`, `folder` (list of room ids), `files` (list of "path  N bytes"), `rooms` (list of `{id, name, parent, recipients, where, path_of_names}`, file texts as stored), `tree_lines` (list of string) |
| `people(ctx)` | `before`, `after` (each `{ per_contact = list of {contact, tops = list of room names}, links = list of "link -> target" }`), `seconds_to_add`, `ritz_recipients` |
| `collision(ctx)` | `variants` = list of `{ variant, links }` for coder |
| `reader(ctx)` | `modes` = list of `{ mode, girlfriend_before, girlfriend_after, coder }`, each view `{ told = list of {room, parent}, lines = list of string }` |
| `log(ctx)` | `t0` (integer), `shapes` = list of `{ shape, results = list of {label, answer}, file_order, screen_order (lists of {written offset, author, text}), bytes, raw, bulk = list of {check, count, bytes, append_seconds, lookup_seconds, found_last, found_unfiled} }` |
| `edits(ctx)` | `window` (string), `rules` = list of `{ rule, results = list of {label, accepted = bool, answer}, screen = list of {text, edited, deleted}, records_in_file, bytes }` |
| `split(ctx)` | `shapes` = list of `{ shape, shared_id, talk_in, seconds, p1_before, p2_before, p1_after, p2_after, p2_old (fork only), live_for_old_id, p2_rooms_before, p2_rooms_after, p2_files_after, p2_links_for_p3 }`; each room state `{ id, name, recipients, people, messages, marker }` |
| `tally(ctx)` | `record` (the gathered options), `counts` |

`ORDER` is the list of `{ key, title }` in the order the demo shows them.
